<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surendranagar district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surendranagar district is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the northern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> peninsula next to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-rann-of-kutch">Little Rann of Kutch</a>. It was formed from many former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a>, among them Wadhwan, Limbdi and Dhrangadhra, which joined the United State of Saurashtra in 1948. Its headquarters, Surendranagar, was formerly Wadhwan Camp.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/surendranagar-district.jpg" alt="Surendranagar district" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emmanuel DYAN from Paris, France · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chotila_-_Chamunda_Devi_Temple,_Gujarat_-_India_(3417734864).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
